# debian/irc-serve.manpages -- which files dh_installman installs, and where from.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS NECESSARY AND NOT OBVIOUS: dh_installman does NOT glob debian/*.1.
# It reads the list of pages from this file (or from debian/tmp, which it searches as a
# fallback) and from its command line, and nothing else. A package that drops
# debian/irc-serve.1 into the packaging directory and assumes debhelper will notice gets
# a .deb with no manual page in it and an `irc-serve --help` that is the only
# documentation a user can find.
#
# MEASURED, and the reason this comment is here rather than a shorter file: the first
# real build of this package had debian/irc-serve.1 and lintian still raised
# `no-manual-page [usr/bin/irc-serve]`, because dh_installman ran, found no list, and
# installed nothing -- silently, with exit 0. dh_installman with this file added exits 0
# and puts irc-serve.1 under debian/irc-serve/usr/share/man/man1/.
#
# `debian/irc-serve.1`, not `irc-serve.1`: dh_installman's search directories are `.` and
# `debian/tmp`, not `debian/`. The bare filename is the version that produces
#   dh_installman: error: Cannot find (any matches for) "irc-serve.1" (tried in ., debian/tmp)
# which is a loud failure, and the loud one is the reason the quiet one was found.
debian/irc-serve.1